\qr \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 God’s Mercy to Israel
\q1 \v 14 “\rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb behold|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb will allure her|מְפַתֶּ֔יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and lead her|וְהֹֽלַכְתִּ֖יהָ\rb* \rb to the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and speak|וְדִבַּרְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to her|עַל\rb* \rb tenderly|לִבָּֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb There|מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I will give back|וְנָתַ֨תִּי\rb* \rb her vineyards|כְּרָמֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb and make the Valley|עֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Achor|עָכ֖וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 2:15 \fqa Achor \ft means \fqa trouble\ft .\f*
\q2 \rb into a gateway|לְפֶ֣תַח\rb* \rb of hope|תִּקְוָ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb There|שָּׁ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb she will respond as she did|וְעָ֤נְתָה\rb*
\q2 \rb in the days|כִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of her youth|נְעוּרֶ֔יהָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb as in the day|וִּכְי֖וֹם\rb* \rb she came up|עֲלֹתָ֥הּ\rb* \rb out|מֵאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃ס\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb |וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb In that|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb day|בַיּוֹם־\rb*,”
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,
\q1 “\rb you will call Me|תִּקְרְאִ֖י\rb* ‘\rb my Husband|אִישִׁ֑י\rb*,’\f + \fr 2:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa my Ishi\f*
\q2 \rb and no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb call|תִקְרְאִי־\rb* \rb Me|לִ֥י\rb* ‘\rb my Master|בַּעְלִֽי׃\rb*.’\f + \fr 2:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa my Baal\f*
\q1 \v 17 \rb For I will remove|וַהֲסִרֹתִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from her lips|מִפִּ֑יהָ\rb* \rb the names|שְׁמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the Baals|הַבְּעָלִ֖ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb will their names|בִּשְׁמָֽם׃\rb* \rb be invoked|יִזָּכְר֥וּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb On that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will make|וְכָרַתִּ֨י\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִית֙\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֤ם\rb*
\q2 \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the beasts|חַיַּ֤ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb and|וְעִם־\rb* \rb the birds|ע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and the creatures that crawl|וְרֶ֖מֶשׂ\rb* \rb on the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb And I will abolish|אֶשְׁבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb bow|וְקֶ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb and sword|וְחֶ֤רֶב\rb*
\q2 \rb and battle|וּמִלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb in|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and will make them lie down|וְהִשְׁכַּבְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb in safety|לָבֶֽטַח׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb So I will betroth you|וְאֵרַשְׂתִּ֥יךְ\rb* \rb to Me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will betroth you|וְאֵרַשְׂתִּ֥יךְ\rb*\rb |לִי֙\rb* \rb in righteousness|בְּצֶ֣דֶק\rb* \rb and justice|וּבְמִשְׁפָּ֔ט\rb*,
\q2 \rb in loving devotion|וּבְחֶ֖סֶד\rb*\f + \fr 2:19 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb and compassion|וּֽבְרַחֲמִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb And I will betroth you|וְאֵרַשְׂתִּ֥יךְ\rb*\rb |לִ֖י\rb* \rb in faithfulness|בֶּאֱמוּנָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and you will know|וְיָדַ֖עַתְּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 21 “\rb |וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will respond|אֶֽעֱנֶה֙\rb* —”
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* —
\q1 “\rb I will respond|אֶעֱנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to the heavens|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and they|וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb will respond|יַעֲנ֥וּ\rb* \rb to the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb And the earth|וְהָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb will respond|תַּעֲנֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the grain|הַדָּגָ֖ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb to the new wine|הַתִּיר֣וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and oil|הַיִּצְהָ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and they|וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb will respond|יַעֲנ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb to Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶֽאל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 2:22 \fqa Jezreel \ft means \fqa God sows\ft .\f*
\q1 \v 23 \rb And I will sow her|וּזְרַעְתִּ֤יהָ\rb* \rb as My own|לִּי֙\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I will have compassion on|וְרִֽחַמְתִּ֖י\rb* ‘\rb No|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb Compassion|רֻחָ֑מָה\rb*.’\f + \fr 2:23 \ft Hebrew \fqa Lo-ruhamah\ft ; LXX \fqa I will love her who was not loved\f*
\q1 \rb I will say to those called|וְאָמַרְתִּ֤י\rb* ‘\rb Not|לְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb My People|עַמִּי־\rb*,’\f + \fr 2:23 \ft Hebrew \fqa Lo-ammi\f*
\q2 ‘\rb You|אַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb are My people|עַמִּי֙\rb*,’\f + \fr 2:23 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 9:25|ROM 9:25\ref* and 1 Peter 2:10\f*
\q1 \rb and they|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb will say|יֹאמַ֥ר\rb*,
\q2 ‘\rb You are my God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃פ\rb*.’”
\c 3
\s1 Hosea Redeems His Wife
\r (\ref Zechariah 2:6–13|ZEC 2:6-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb show love|אֱ‍ֽהַב־\rb* \rb to your wife|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb again|ע֚וֹד\rb*, \rb though she is loved|אֲהֻ֥בַת\rb* \rb by another|רֵ֖עַ\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Or \fqa Go show love to a woman who is loved by another\f* \rb and is an adulteress|וּמְנָאָ֑פֶת\rb*. \rb Love her|כְּאַהֲבַ֤ת\rb* \rb as the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb loves|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb though they|וְהֵ֗ם\rb* \rb turn|פֹּנִים֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb and love to offer|וְאֹהֲבֵ֖י\rb* \rb raisin cakes to idols|אֲשִׁישֵׁ֥י\rb*\rb |עֲנָבִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Literally \fqa and love raisin cakes\f*”
\p \v 2 \rb So I bought her|וָאֶכְּרֶ֣הָ\rb*\rb |לִּ֔י\rb* \rb for fifteen shekels|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb of silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 3:2 \fqa 15 shekels \ft is approximately 6 ounces or 171 grams of silver.\f* \rb and a homer|וְחֹ֥מֶר\rb* \rb and a lethech|וְלֵ֥תֶךְ\rb*\rb |שְׂעֹרִֽים׃\rb* \rb of barley|שְׂעֹרִ֖ים\rb*.\f + \fr 3:2 \ft Or \fqa a homer and a half of barley\ft ; that is, a total of approximately 9.36 bushels or 330 liters (probably about 436 pounds or 198 kilograms of barley); LXX \fqa a homer of barley and a wineskin full of wine\f* \v 3 \rb Then I said|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֗יהָ\rb*, “\rb You must live|תֵּ֣שְׁבִי\rb* \rb with me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb for many|רַבִּים֙\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֤ים\rb*; \rb you must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be promiscuous|תִזְנִ֔י\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or belong to|תִֽהְיִ֖י\rb* \rb another|לְאִ֑ישׁ\rb*, \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will do the same for you|אֵלָֽיִךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb must live|יֵֽשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֗ים\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb without|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb king|מֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb or prince|שָׂ֔ר\rb*, \rb without|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb sacrifice|זֶ֖בַח\rb* \rb or|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb sacred pillar|מַצֵּבָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and without|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb ephod|אֵפ֖וֹד\rb* \rb or idol|וּתְרָפִֽים׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Afterward|אַחַ֗ר\rb*, \rb the people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb will return|יָשֻׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb and seek|וּבִקְשׁוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb their king|מַלְכָּ֑ם\rb*. \rb They will come trembling|וּפָחֲד֧וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb His goodness|טוּב֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the last|בְּאַחֲרִ֥ית\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִֽים׃פ\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 God’s Case against His People
\q1 \v 1 \rb Hear|שִׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb O children|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*,
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb has a case|רִ֤יב\rb*
\q2 \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the people|יוֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb |כִּ֠י\rb* \rb There is no|אֵין־\rb* \rb truth|אֱמֶ֧ת\rb*, \rb no|וְֽאֵין־\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֛סֶד\rb*,
\q2 \rb and no|וְאֵֽין־\rb* \rb knowledge|דַּ֥עַת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 2 \rb Cursing|אָלֹ֣ה\rb* \rb and lying|וְכַחֵ֔שׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb murder|וְרָצֹ֥חַ\rb* \rb and stealing|וְגָנֹ֖ב\rb*,
\q1 \rb and adultery|וְנָאֹ֑ף\rb* \rb are rampant|פָּרָ֕צוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb one act of bloodshed|וְדָמִ֥ים\rb*\rb |בְּדָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb follows another|נָגָֽעוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֣ן׀\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb mourns|תֶּאֱבַ֣ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who dwell|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in it|בָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb will waste away|וְאֻמְלַל֙\rb*
\q1 \rb with the beasts|בְּחַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb and the birds|וּבְע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb*;
\q2 \rb even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb the fish|דְּגֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb disappear|יֵאָסֵֽפוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb But|אַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb let no|אַל־\rb* \rb man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb contend|יָרֵ֖ב\rb*;
\q2 \rb let no|וְאַל־\rb* \rb man|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb offer reproof|יוֹכַ֣ח\rb*;
\q1 \rb for your people are like those|וְעַמְּךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb who contend with|כִּמְרִיבֵ֥י\rb* \rb a priest|כֹהֵֽן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 4:4 \ft Or \fqa for My case is against you, O priests\f*
\q1 \v 5 \rb You will stumble|וְכָשַׁלְתָּ֣\rb* \rb by day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the prophet|נָבִ֛יא\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb will stumble|וְכָשַׁ֧ל\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb by night|לָ֑יְלָה\rb*;
\q2 \rb so I will destroy|וְדָמִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb your mother|אִמֶּֽךָ׃\rb* —
\q1 \v 6 \rb My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb are destroyed|נִדְמ֥וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb for lack|מִבְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb of knowledge|הַדָּ֑עַת\rb*.
\q1 \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb have rejected|מָאַ֗סְתָּ\rb* \rb knowledge|הַדַּ֣עַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb I will also reject you|וְאֶמְאָֽסְאךָ֙\rb* \rb as My priests|מִכַּהֵ֣ן\rb*.
\q1 \rb Since you have forgotten|וַתִּשְׁכַּח֙\rb* \rb the law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb will also|גַּם־\rb* \rb forget|אֶשְׁכַּ֥ח\rb* \rb your children|בָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb The more they multiplied|כְּרֻבָּ֖ם\rb*,\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb*
\q2 \rb the more they sinned|חָֽטְאוּ־\rb* \rb against Me|לִ֑י\rb*;
\q1 \rb they exchanged|אָמִֽיר׃\rb* \rb their Glory|כְּבוֹדָ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 4:7 \ft Or \fqa they exchanged their glorious God \ft (Syriac); MT \fqa I will exchange their glory\f*
\q2 \rb for a thing of disgrace|בְּקָל֥וֹן\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb They feed on|יֹאכֵ֑לוּ\rb* \rb the sins|חַטַּ֥את\rb*\f + \fr 4:8 \ft Or \fqa the sin offerings\f* \rb of My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb and set|יִשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb their hearts|נַפְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb* \rb on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb iniquity|עֲוֺנָ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb And it shall be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb*
\q2 \rb like people|כָעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb like priest|כַּכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will punish|וּפָקַדְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb both of them|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb for their ways|דְּרָכָ֔יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and repay|אָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb them|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb for their deeds|וּמַעֲלָלָ֖יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb They will eat|וְאָֽכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb but not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb be satisfied|יִשְׂבָּ֔עוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb they will be promiscuous|הִזְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb but not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb multiply|יִפְרֹ֑צוּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb they have abandoned|עָזְב֖וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb to give themselves|לִשְׁמֹֽר׃\rb*
\q2 \v 11 \rb to promiscuity|זְנ֛וּת\rb*, \rb wine|וְיַ֥יִן\rb*, \rb and new wine|וְתִיר֖וֹשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb which take away|יִֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb understanding|לֵֽב׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb My people|עַמִּי֙\rb* \rb consult|יִשְׁאָ֔ל\rb* \rb their wooden idols|בְּעֵצ֣וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and their divining rods|וּמַקְל֖וֹ\rb* \rb inform|יַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb them|ל֑וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb a spirit|ר֤וּחַ\rb* \rb of prostitution|זְנוּנִים֙\rb* \rb leads them astray|הִתְעָ֔ה\rb*
