\q1 \v 5 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb I have hewn them|חָצַ֙בְתִּי֙\rb* \rb by the prophets|בַּנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb I have slain them|הֲרַגְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb by the words|בְּאִמְרֵי־\rb* \rb of My mouth|פִ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and My judgments|וּמִשְׁפָּטֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb go forth|יֵצֵֽא׃\rb* \rb like lightning|א֥וֹר\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I desire|חָפַ֖צְתִּי\rb* \rb mercy|חֶ֥סֶד\rb*, \rb not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb sacrifice|זָ֑בַח\rb*,\f + \fr 6:6 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 9:13|MAT 9:13\ref* and Matthew 12:7\f*
\q2 \rb and the knowledge|וְדַ֥עַת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb rather than burnt offerings|מֵעֹלֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb But they|וְהֵ֕מָּה\rb*, \rb like Adam|כְּאָדָ֖ם\rb*, \rb have transgressed|עָבְר֣וּ\rb*\f + \fr 6:7 \ft Or \fqa As at Adam, they have transgressed\f* \rb the covenant|בְרִ֑ית\rb*;
\q2 \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb they were unfaithful|בָּ֥גְדוּ\rb* \rb to Me|בִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Gilead|גִּלְעָ֕ד\rb* \rb is a city|קִרְיַ֖ת\rb* \rb of evildoers|פֹּ֣עֲלֵי\rb*\rb |אָ֑וֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb tracked with footprints|עֲקֻבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb of blood|מִדָּֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb Like raiders|גְּדוּדִ֗ים\rb* \rb who lie in ambush|וּכְחַכֵּ֨י\rb*\rb |אִ֜ישׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb so does a band|חֶ֚בֶר\rb* \rb of priests|כֹּֽהֲנִ֔ים\rb*;
\q1 \rb they murder|יְרַצְּחוּ־\rb* \rb on the way|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb to Shechem|שֶׁ֑כְמָה\rb*;
\q2 \rb surely|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they have committed|עָשֽׂוּ׃\rb* \rb atrocities|זִמָּ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb In the house|בְּבֵית֙\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*
\q2 \rb I have seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb a horrible thing|שַׁעֲרִירִיָּה\rb*:
\q1 \rb Ephraim|לְאֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb practices prostitution|זְנ֣וּת\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֚ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb is defiled|נִטְמָ֖א\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Also|גַּם־\rb* \rb for you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb O Judah|יְהוּדָ֕ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb a harvest|קָצִ֖יר\rb* \rb is appointed|שָׁ֥ת\rb*,
\q1 \rb when I restore|בְּשׁוּבִ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb My people|עַמִּֽי׃פ\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁב֥וּת\rb*.\f + \fr 6:11 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of My people\f*
\c 7
\s1 Ephraim’s Iniquity
\q1 \v 1 \rb When I heal|כְּרָפְאִ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֤ן\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*\f + \fr 7:1 \ft That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verses 8 and 11\f* \rb will be exposed|וְנִגְלָ֞ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb as well as the crimes|וְרָע֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹֽׁמְר֔וֹן\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they practice|פָעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb deceit|שָׁ֑קֶר\rb* \rb and thieves|וְגַנָּ֣ב\rb* \rb break in|יָב֔וֹא\rb*;
\q2 \rb bandits|גְּד֖וּד\rb* \rb raid|פָּשַׁ֥ט\rb* \rb in the streets|בַּחֽוּץ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb But they fail to|וּבַל־\rb* \rb consider|יֹֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb in their hearts|לִלְבָבָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb that I remember|זָכָ֑רְתִּי\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their evil|רָעָתָ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb Now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb their deeds|מַֽעַלְלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb are all around them|סְבָב֣וּם\rb*;
\q2 \rb they are|הָיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb before|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַ֖י\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb They delight|יְשַׂמְּחוּ־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb with their evil|בְּרָעָתָ֖ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the princes|שָׂרִֽים׃\rb* \rb with their lies|וּבְכַחֲשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb They are all|כֻּלָּם֙\rb* \rb adulterers|מְנָ֣אֲפִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb like|כְּמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb an oven|תַנּ֔וּר\rb* \rb heated|בֹּעֵ֖רָה\rb* \rb by a baker|מֵֽאֹפֶ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb who needs not|יִשְׁבּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb stoke the fire|מֵעִ֔יר\rb*
\q2 \rb from the kneading|מִלּ֥וּשׁ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the rising|חֻמְצָתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb of the dough|בָּצֵ֖ק\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb The princes|שָׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb are inflamed|הֶחֱל֥וּ\rb*\rb |חֲמַ֣ת\rb* \rb with wine|מִיָּ֑יִן\rb*
\q2 \rb on the day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of our king|מַלְכֵּ֔נוּ\rb*;
\q1 \rb so he joins hands|מָשַׁ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |יָד֖וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those who mock him|לֹצְצִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they prepare|קֵרְב֧וּ\rb* \rb their heart|לִבָּ֖ם\rb* \rb like an oven|כַתַּנּ֛וּר\rb*
\q2 \rb while they lie in wait|בְּאָרְבָּ֑ם\rb*;
\q1 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb night|הַלַּ֙יְלָה֙\rb* \rb their anger|אֹֽפֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb smolders|יָשֵׁ֣ן\rb*;\f + \fr 7:6 \ft Literally \fqa their baker sleeps\f*
\q2 \rb in the morning|בֹּ֕קֶר\rb* \rb it|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb blazes|בֹעֵ֖ר\rb* \rb like a flaming|לֶהָבָֽה׃\rb* \rb fire|כְּאֵ֥שׁ\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb All|כֻּלָּ֤ם\rb* \rb of them are hot|יֵחַ֙מּוּ֙\rb* \rb as an oven|כַּתַּנּ֔וּר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and they devour|וְאָכְל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their rulers|שֹֽׁפְטֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb their kings|מַלְכֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb fall|נָפָ֔לוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb not one|אֵין־\rb* \rb of them|בָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb calls|קֹרֵ֥א\rb* \rb upon Me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֕יִם\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb mixes|יִתְבּוֹלָ֑ל\rb* \rb with the nations|בָּעַמִּ֖ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb is|הָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |בְּלִ֥י\rb* \rb an unturned|הֲפוּכָֽה׃\rb* \rb cake|עֻגָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb Foreigners|זָרִים֙\rb* \rb consume|אָכְל֤וּ\rb* \rb his strength|כֹּח֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb notice|יָדָ֑ע\rb*.
\q1 \rb Even|גַּם־\rb* \rb his hair is streaked|זָ֣רְקָה\rb* \rb with gray|שֵׂיבָה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb know|יָדָֽע׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb arrogance|גְאֽוֹן־\rb* \rb testifies|וְעָנָ֥ה\rb* \rb against them|בְּפָנָ֑יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb yet they do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb return|שָׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb despite all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb this|זֹֽאת׃\rb*, \rb they do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb seek Him|בִקְשֻׁ֖הוּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb So Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb has become|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb like a silly|פוֹתָ֖ה\rb*, \rb senseless|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |לֵ֑ב\rb* \rb dove|כְּיוֹנָ֥ה\rb* —
\q2 \rb calling out|קָרָ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֥יִם\rb*, \rb then turning|הָלָֽכוּ׃\rb* \rb to Assyria|אַשּׁ֥וּר\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they go|יֵלֵ֗כוּ\rb*, \rb I will spread|אֶפְר֤וֹשׂ\rb* \rb My net|רִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will bring them down|אֽוֹרִידֵ֑ם\rb* \rb like birds|כְּע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will chastise them|אַיְסִרֵ֕ם\rb*
\q2 \rb when I hear them|כְּשֵׁ֖מַע\rb* \rb flocking together|לַעֲדָתָֽם׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 7:12 \ft Or \fqa I will chastise them according to what was reported against them in the assembly.\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Woe|א֤וֹי\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶם֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they have strayed|נָדְד֣וּ\rb* \rb from Me|מִמֶּ֔נִּי\rb*!
\q2 \rb Destruction|שֹׁ֥ד\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they have rebelled|פָ֣שְׁעוּ\rb* \rb against Me|בִ֑י\rb*!
\q1 \rb Though I|וְאָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb would redeem them|אֶפְדֵּ֔ם\rb*,\rb |וְהֵ֕מָּה\rb*
\q2 \rb they speak|דִּבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb lies|כְּזָבִֽים׃\rb* \rb against Me|עָלַ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb They do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb cry out|זָעֲק֤וּ\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb from their hearts|בְּלִבָּ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb when|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they wail|יְיֵלִ֖ילוּ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb their beds|מִשְׁכְּבוֹתָ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb They slash themselves|יִתְגּוֹרָ֖רוּ\rb*\f + \fr 7:14 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts and LXX; see \ref 1 Kings 18:28|1KI 18:28\ref*. Most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa They gather together\f* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb grain|דָּגָ֧ן\rb* \rb and new wine|וְתִיר֛וֹשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but turn away|יָס֥וּרוּ\rb* \rb from Me|בִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb Although I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb trained|יִסַּ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb and strengthened|חִזַּ֖קְתִּי\rb* \rb their arms|זְרֽוֹעֹתָ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb they plot|יְחַשְּׁבוּ־\rb* \rb evil|רָֽע׃\rb* \rb against Me|וְאֵלַ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb They turn|יָשׁ֣וּבוּ׀\rb*, \rb but not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to the Most High|עָ֗ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb they are|הָיוּ֙\rb* \rb like a faulty|רְמִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb bow|כְּקֶ֣שֶׁת\rb*.
\q1 \rb Their leaders|שָׂרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will fall|יִפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בַחֶ֛רֶב\rb*
\q2 \rb for the cursing|מִזַּ֣עַם\rb* \rb of their tongue|לְשׁוֹנָ֑ם\rb*;
\q1 \rb for this|ז֥וֹ\rb* \rb they will be ridiculed|לַעְגָּ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\c 8
\s1 Israel Will Reap the Whirlwind
\q1 \v 1 \rb Put the ram’s horn|שֹׁפָ֔ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your lips|חִכְּךָ֣\rb*!
\q2 \rb An eagle|כַּנֶּ֖שֶׁר\rb* \rb looms over|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb because|יַ֚עַן\rb* \rb the people have transgressed|עָבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb My covenant|בְרִיתִ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb and rebelled|פָּשָֽׁעוּ׃\rb* \rb against|וְעַל־\rb* \rb My law|תּוֹרָתִ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb cries out|יִזְעָ֑קוּ\rb* \rb to Me|לִ֖י\rb*,
\q2 “\rb O our God|אֱלֹהַ֥י\rb*, \rb we know You|יְֽדַעֲנ֖וּךָ\rb*!”
\q1 \v 3 \rb But Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb has rejected|זָנַ֥ח\rb* \rb good|ט֑וֹב\rb*;
\q2 \rb an enemy|אוֹיֵ֖ב\rb* \rb will pursue him|יִרְדְּֽפוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb They|הֵ֤ם\rb* \rb set up kings|הִמְלִיכוּ֙\rb*, \rb but not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb by Me|מִמֶּ֔נִּי\rb*.
\q2 \rb They make princes|הֵשִׂ֖ירוּ\rb*, \rb but without|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb My approval|יָדָ֑עְתִּי\rb*.
\q1 \rb With their silver|כַּסְפָּ֣ם\rb* \rb and gold|וּזְהָבָ֗ם\rb* \rb they make|עָשׂ֤וּ\rb* \rb themselves|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb idols|עֲצַבִּ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb to|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb their own destruction|יִכָּרֵֽת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb He has rejected|זָנַח֙\rb* \rb your calf|עֶגְלֵ֣ךְ\rb*,\f + \fr 8:5 \ft Or \fqa calf idol\ft ; see \ref 1 Kings 12:29|1KI 12:29\ref*.\f* \rb O Samaria|שֹֽׁמְר֔וֹן\rb*.
\q2 \rb My anger|אַפִּ֖י\rb* \rb burns|חָרָ֥ה\rb* \rb against them|בָּ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb How long will they be|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַ֕י\rb*
\q2 \rb incapable|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |יוּכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb of innocence|נִקָּיֹֽן׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb this thing|וְה֔וּא\rb* \rb is from Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*—
\q2 \rb a craftsman|חָרָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb made it|עָשָׂ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and it|ה֑וּא\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb is not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb It will be|יִֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb broken to pieces|שְׁבָבִ֣ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb that calf|עֵ֖גֶל\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they sow|יִזְרָ֖עוּ\rb* \rb the wind|ר֥וּחַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and they shall reap|יִקְצֹ֑רוּ\rb* \rb the whirlwind|וְסוּפָ֣תָה\rb*.
\q1 \rb There is no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb standing grain|קָמָ֣ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb what sprouts|צֶ֚מַח\rb* \rb fails|בְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb to yield|יַֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb flour|קֶּ֔מַח\rb*.
\q1 \rb Even if|אוּלַ֣י\rb* \rb it should produce|יַֽעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb the foreigners|זָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb would swallow it up|יִבְלָעֻֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb is swallowed up|נִבְלַ֖ע\rb*!
\q2 \rb Now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb they are|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb among the nations|בַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb like a worthless|אֵֽין־\rb*\rb |חֵ֥פֶץ\rb* \rb vessel|כִּכְלִ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb have gone up|עָל֣וּ\rb* \rb to Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb*
\q2 \rb like a wild donkey|פֶּ֖רֶא\rb* \rb on its own|בּוֹדֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb*.
\q2 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb*\f + \fr 8:9 \ft That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verse 11\f* \rb has hired|הִתְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb lovers|אֲהָבִֽים\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Though|גַּ֛ם\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they hire allies|יִתְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb among the nations|בַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb I will now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb round them up|אֲקַבְּצֵ֑ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb and they will begin|וַיָּחֵ֣לּוּ\rb* \rb to diminish|מְּעָ֔ט\rb*
\q2 \rb under the oppression|מִמַּשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of princes|שָׂרִֽים׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb multiplied|הִרְבָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the altars|מִזְבְּחֹ֖ת\rb* \rb for sin|לַחֲטֹ֑א\rb*,
\q2 \rb they became|הָיוּ־\rb* \rb his|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּח֖וֹת\rb* \rb for sinning|לַחֲטֹֽא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Though I wrote for them|אֶכְתּוֹב\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb the great things|רִבּוֹ\rb* \rb of My law|תּֽוֹרָתִ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb they regarded them|נֶחְשָֽׁבוּ׃\rb* \rb as|כְּמוֹ־\rb* \rb something strange|זָ֖ר\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb Though they offer|יִזְבְּח֤וּ\rb* \rb sacrifices|זִבְחֵ֣י\rb* \rb as gifts to Me|הַבְהָבַ֗י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and though they eat|וַיֹּאכֵ֔לוּ\rb* \rb the meat|בָשָׂר֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb accept them|רָצָ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb Now|עַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb He will remember|יִזְכֹּ֤ר\rb* \rb their iniquity|עֲוֺנָם֙\rb* \rb and punish|וְיִפְקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb their sins|חַטֹּאותָ֔ם\rb*:
\q2 \rb They|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb will return|יָשֽׁוּבוּ׃\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֥יִם\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has forgotten|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֨ח\rb* \rb his Maker|עֹשֵׂ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and built|וַיִּ֙בֶן֙\rb* \rb palaces|הֵֽיכָל֔וֹת\rb*;
\q2 \rb Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֕ה\rb* \rb has multiplied|הִרְבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb its fortified|בְּצֻר֑וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb But I will send|וְשִׁלַּחְתִּי־\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb upon their cities|בְּעָרָ֔יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and it will consume|וְאָכְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb their citadels|אַרְמְנֹתֶֽיהָ׃ס\rb*.
\c 9
\s1 Israel’s Punishment
\q1 \v 1 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb rejoice|תִּשְׂמַ֨ח\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb exultation|גִּיל֙\rb* \rb like the nations|כָּֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have played the harlot|זָנִ֖יתָ\rb* \rb against|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb you have made love|אָהַ֣בְתָּ\rb* \rb for hire|אֶתְנָ֔ן\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb threshing floor|גָּרְנ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |דָּגָֽן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb The threshing floor|גֹּ֥רֶן\rb* \rb and winepress|וָיֶ֖קֶב\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb feed them|יִרְעֵ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the new wine|וְתִיר֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb will fail them|יְכַ֥חֶשׁ\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb They will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb remain|יֵשְׁב֖וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*;
\q1 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*\f + \fr 9:3 \ft That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; similarly in verses 8, 11, 13, and 16\f* \rb will return|וְשָׁ֤ב\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and eat|יֹאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb unclean food|טָמֵ֥א\rb* \rb in Assyria|וּבְאַשּׁ֖וּר\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb They will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb pour out|יִסְּכ֨וּ\rb* \rb wine offerings|יַיִן֮\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb and their sacrifices|זִבְחֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb please|יֶֽעֶרְבוּ־\rb* \rb Him|לוֹ֒\rb*,
\q1 \rb but will be to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb like the bread|כְּלֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb of mourners|אוֹנִים֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who eat|אֹכְלָ֖יו\rb* \rb will be defiled|יִטַמָּ֑אוּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their bread|לַחְמָ֣ם\rb* \rb will be for themselves|לְנַפְשָׁ֔ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb it will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb enter|יָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb What|מַֽה־\rb* \rb will you do|תַּעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb on the appointed|מוֹעֵ֑ד\rb* \rb day|לְי֣וֹם\rb*,
\q2 \rb on the day|וּלְי֖וֹם\rb* \rb of the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb feast|חַג־\rb*?
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb even if|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb they flee|הָֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb destruction|מִשֹּׁ֔ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֥יִם\rb* \rb will gather them|תְּקַבְּצֵ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and Memphis|מֹ֣ף\rb* \rb will bury them|תְּקַבְּרֵ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb Their precious|מַחְמַ֣ד\rb* \rb silver|לְכַסְפָּ֗ם\rb* \rb will be taken over|יִֽירָשֵׁ֔ם\rb* \rb by thistles|קִמּוֹשׂ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and thorns will overrun|ח֖וֹחַ\rb* \rb their tents|בְּאָהֳלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb The days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of punishment|הַפְּקֻדָּ֗ה\rb* \rb have come|בָּ֣אוּ׀\rb*;
\q2 \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of retribution|הַשִׁלֻּ֔ם\rb* \rb have arrived|בָּ֚אוּ\rb* —
\q2 \rb let Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb know it|יֵדְע֖וּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb The prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb* \rb is called a fool|אֱוִ֣יל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the inspired|הָר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb insane|מְשֻׁגָּע֙\rb*,
\q1 \rb because of|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the greatness|רֹ֣ב\rb*
\q2 \rb of your iniquity|עֲוֺנְךָ֔\rb*\rb |וְרַבָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and hostility|מַשְׂטֵמָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb The prophet|נָבִ֞יא\rb* \rb is Ephraim’s|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb watchman|צֹפֶ֥ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb along with|עִם־\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb*,\f + \fr 9:8 \ft Or \fqa The prophet is the watchman over Ephraim, the people of my God\f*
\q1 \rb yet the snare|פַּ֤ח\rb* \rb of the fowler|יָקוֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb lies on|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his paths|דְּרָכָ֔יו\rb*.
\q2 \rb Hostility|מַשְׂטֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb is in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of his God|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 9 \rb They have deeply|הֶעְמִֽיקוּ־\rb* \rb corrupted themselves|שִׁחֵ֖תוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb as in the days|כִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gibeah|הַגִּבְעָ֑ה\rb*;
\q1 \rb He will remember|יִזְכּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb their guilt|עֲוֺנָ֔ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb He will punish|יִפְק֖וֹד\rb* \rb their sins|חַטֹּאותָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb I found|מָצָ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb like grapes|כַּעֲנָבִ֣ים\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֗ר\rb*.
\q2 \rb I saw|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb as the firstfruits|כְּבִכּוּרָ֤ה\rb*
\q2 \rb of the fig tree|בִתְאֵנָה֙\rb* \rb in its first season|בְּרֵ֣אשִׁיתָ֔הּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb But they|הֵ֜מָּה\rb* \rb went|בָּ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |בַֽעַל־\rb* \rb to Baal-peor|פְּע֗וֹר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and consecrated|וַיִּנָּֽזְרוּ֙\rb* \rb themselves to Shame|לַבֹּ֔שֶׁת\rb*;
\q1 \rb so they became|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb as detestable|שִׁקּוּצִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb as the thing they loved|כְּאָהֳבָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb Ephraim’s|אֶפְרַ֕יִם\rb* \rb glory|כְּבוֹדָ֑ם\rb* \rb will fly away|יִתְעוֹפֵ֣ף\rb* \rb like a bird|כָּע֖וֹף\rb*,
\q2 \rb with no birth|מִלֵּדָ֥ה\rb*, \rb no pregnancy|וּמִבֶּ֖טֶן\rb*, \rb and no conception|וּמֵהֵרָיֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Even|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb they raise|יְגַדְּלוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their children|בְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb I will bereave them|וְשִׁכַּלְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb of each one|מֵֽאָדָ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb Yes|כִּֽי־\rb*,\rb |גַם־\rb* \rb woe be|א֥וֹי\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb when I turn away|בְּשׂוּרִ֥י\rb* \rb from them|מֵהֶֽם׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 13 \rb I have seen|רָאִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֛יִם\rb*, \rb like|כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Tyre|לְצ֖וֹר\rb*,
\q2 \rb planted|שְׁתוּלָ֣ה\rb* \rb in a meadow|בְנָוֶ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb But Ephraim|וְאֶפְרַ֕יִם\rb* \rb will bring out|לְהוֹצִ֥יא\rb*
\q2 \rb his children|בָּנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb for slaughter|הֹרֵ֖ג\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb Give|תֵּן־\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֥ם\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*—
\q2 \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb will You give|תִּתֵּ֑ן\rb*?
\q1 \rb Give|תֵּן־\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb wombs|רֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb that miscarry|מַשְׁכִּ֔יל\rb*
\q2 \rb and breasts|וְשָׁדַ֖יִם\rb* \rb that dry up|צֹמְקִֽים׃\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb their evil|רָעָתָ֤ם\rb* \rb appears at Gilgal|בַּגִּלְגָּל֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb I hated them|שְׂנֵאתִ֔ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will drive them|אֲגָרְשֵׁ֑ם\rb* \rb from My house|מִבֵּיתִ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb for|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the wickedness|רֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb of their deeds|מַֽעַלְלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will no|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb longer|אוֹסֵף֙\rb* \rb love them|אַהֲבָתָ֔ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their leaders|שָׂרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb are rebellious|סֹרְרִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb is struck down|הֻכָּ֣ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb their root|שָׁרְשָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb is withered|יָבֵ֖שׁ\rb*;
\q2 \rb they cannot bear|יַעֲשׂ֑וּן\rb* \rb fruit|פְּרִ֣י\rb*.\rb |בְלִי\rb*
\q1 \rb Even|גַּ֚ם\rb* \rb if|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they bear children|יֵֽלֵד֔וּן\rb*,
\q2 \rb I will slay|וְהֵמַתִּ֖י\rb* \rb the darlings|מַחֲמַדֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of their wombs|בִטְנָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb My God|אֱלֹהַ֔י\rb* \rb will reject them|יִמְאָסֵ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they have not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb obeyed|שָׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb Him|ל֑וֹ\rb*;
\q1 \rb and they shall be|וְיִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb wanderers|נֹדְדִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִֽם׃ס\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 Retribution for Israel’s Sin
\q1 \v 1 \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb was a luxuriant|בּוֹקֵק֙\rb* \rb vine|גֶּ֤פֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb yielding|יְשַׁוֶּה־\rb* \rb fruit|פְּרִ֖י\rb* \rb for himself|לּ֑וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \rb The more his fruit|לְפִרְי֗וֹ\rb* \rb increased|כְּרֹ֣ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb the more he increased|הִרְבָּה֙\rb* \rb the altars|לַֽמִּזְבְּח֔וֹת\rb*.
\q1 \rb The better|כְּט֣וֹב\rb* \rb his land produced|לְאַרְצ֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb the better he made|הֵיטִ֖יבוּ\rb* \rb the sacred pillars|מַצֵּבֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb Their hearts|לִבָּ֖ם\rb* \rb are devious|חָלַ֥ק\rb*;
\q2 \rb now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb they must bear their guilt|יֶאְשָׁ֑מוּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb The LORD|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will break down|יַעֲרֹ֣ף\rb* \rb their altars|מִזְבְּחוֹתָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and demolish|יְשֹׁדֵ֖ד\rb* \rb their sacred pillars|מַצֵּבוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Surely|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb they will say|יֹֽאמְר֔וּ\rb*,
\q2 “\rb We have|לָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*,
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb we do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb revere|יָרֵ֙אנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהֹוָ֔ה\rb*.
\q2 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb can a king|וְהַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb do|יַּֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for us|לָּֽנוּ׃\rb*?”
\q1 \v 4 \rb They speak|דִּבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb mere words|דְבָרִ֔ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb with false|שָׁ֖וְא\rb* \rb oaths|אָל֥וֹת\rb* \rb they make|כָּרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb covenants|בְּרִ֑ית\rb*.
\q1 \rb So judgment|מִשְׁפָּ֔ט\rb* \rb springs up|וּפָרַ֤ח\rb*
\q2 \rb like poisonous weeds|כָּרֹאשׁ֙\rb* \rb in|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the furrows|תַּלְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of a field|שָׂדָֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb The people|שְׁכַ֣ן\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹֽׁמְר֑וֹן\rb* \rb will fear|יָג֖וּרוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb for the calf|לְעֶגְלוֹת֙\rb* \rb of|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Beth-aven|אָ֔וֶן\rb*.\f + \fr 10:5 \fqa Beth-aven \ft means \fqa house of wickedness\ft . This is a derogatory term for Bethel, which means \fqa house of God\ft ; see \ref 1 Kings 12:28–29|1KI 12:28-29\ref*.\f*
\q1 \rb Indeed|כִּי־\rb*, \rb its people|עַמּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb will mourn|אָבַ֨ל\rb* \rb over it|עָלָ֜יו\rb*
\q2 \rb with its idolatrous priests|וּכְמָרָיו֙\rb* —
\q1 \rb those who rejoiced|יָגִ֔ילוּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb its glory|כְּבוֹד֖וֹ\rb* —
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it has been taken from them into exile|גָלָ֥ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Yes|גַּם־\rb*,\rb |אוֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb it will be carried|יוּבָ֔ל\rb* \rb to Assyria|לְאַשּׁ֣וּר\rb*
\q2 \rb as tribute|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the great|יָרֵ֑ב\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*.\f + \fr 10:6 \ft Or \fqa to King Jareb\f*
\q1 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֣יִם\rb*\f + \fr 10:6 \ft That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verse 11\f* \rb will be seized|יִקָּ֔ח\rb* \rb with shame|בָּשְׁנָה֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb will be ashamed|וְיֵב֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb of its wooden idols|מֵעֲצָתֽוֹ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 10:6 \ft Or \fqa of its own counsel\f*
\q1 \v 7 \rb Samaria|שֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb will be carried off|נִדְמֶ֥ה\rb* \rb with her king|מַלְכָּ֑הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb like a twig|כְּקֶ֖צֶף\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the surface|פְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of the water|מָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb The high places|בָּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Aven|אָ֗וֶן\rb*\f + \fr 10:8 \ft Or \fqa of wickedness\ft ; \fqa Aven \ft is a reference to Beth-aven (a derogatory term for Bethel); see verse 5.\f* \rb will be destroyed|וְנִשְׁמְד֞וּ\rb*—
\q2 \rb it is the sin|חַטַּאת֙\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb thorns|ק֣וֹץ\rb* \rb and thistles|וְדַרְדַּ֔ר\rb* \rb will overgrow|יַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb their altars|מִזְבְּחוֹתָ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb Then they will say|וְאָמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb to the mountains|לֶֽהָרִים֙\rb*, “\rb Cover us|כַּסּ֔וּנוּ\rb*!”
\q2 \rb and to the hills|וְלַגְּבָע֖וֹת\rb*, “\rb Fall|נִפְל֥וּ\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵֽינוּ׃ס\rb*!”\f + \fr 10:8 \ft Cited in \ref Luke 23:30|LUK 23:30\ref*; see also Revelation 6:16.\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Since the days|מִימֵי֙\rb* \rb of Gibeah|הַגִּבְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb you have sinned|חָטָ֖אתָ\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb you have remained|עָמָ֔דוּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb the battle|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Gibeah|בַּגִּבְעָ֛ה\rb*
\q2 \rb overtake|תַשִּׂיגֵ֧ם\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of iniquity|עַֽלְוָֽה׃\rb*?\f + \fr 10:9 \ft Or \fqa Did not the battle overtake the sons of iniquity in Gibeah?\f*
\q1 \v 10 \rb I will chasten them|וְאֶסֳּרֵ֑ם\rb* \rb when I please|בְּאַוָּתִ֖י\rb*;
\q2 \rb nations|עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb will be gathered|וְאֻסְּפ֤וּ\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*
\q1 \rb to put them in bondage|בְּאָסְרָ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb for their double|לִשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb transgression|עֵינֹתָם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Ephraim|וְאֶפְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb is a well-trained|מְלֻמָּדָה֙\rb* \rb heifer|עֶגְלָ֤ה\rb* \rb that loves|אֹהַ֣בְתִּי\rb* \rb to thresh|לָד֔וּשׁ\rb*;
\q2 \rb but I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb will place a yoke|עָבַ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb her fair|ט֖וּב\rb* \rb neck|צַוָּארָ֑הּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will harness|אַרְכִּ֤יב\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb will plow|יַחֲר֣וֹשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and Jacob|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \rb will break the hard ground|יְשַׂדֶּד־\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Sow|זִרְע֨וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb righteousness|לִצְדָקָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and reap the fruit|קִצְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb of loving devotion|חֶ֔סֶד\rb*;
\q2 \rb break up|נִ֥ירוּ\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb unplowed ground|נִ֑יר\rb*.
\q1 \rb For it is time|וְעֵת֙\rb* \rb to seek|לִדְר֣וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb He comes|יָב֕וֹא\rb* \rb and sends righteousness|צֶ֖דֶק\rb*
\q2 \rb upon you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb like rain|וְיֹרֶ֥ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb You have plowed|חֲרַשְׁתֶּם־\rb* \rb wickedness|רֶ֛שַׁע\rb* \rb and reaped|קְצַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb injustice|עַוְלָ֥תָה\rb*;
\q2 \rb you have eaten|אֲכַלְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb the fruit|פְּרִי־\rb* \rb of lies|כָ֑חַשׁ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have trusted|בָטַ֥חְתָּ\rb* \rb in your own way|בְדַרְכְּךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb and in the multitude|בְּרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb of your mighty men|גִּבּוֹרֶֽיךָ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 14 \rb the roar of battle|שָׁאוֹן֮\rb* \rb will rise|וְקָ֣אם\rb* \rb against your people|בְּעַמֶּךָ֒\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your fortresses|מִבְצָרֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb will be demolished|יוּשַּׁ֔ד\rb*
\q1 \rb as Shalman|שַֽׁלְמַ֛ן\rb* \rb devastated|כְּשֹׁ֧ד\rb* \rb Beth-arbel|אַֽרְבֵ֖אל\rb*
\q2 \rb in the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of battle|מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb when mothers|אֵ֥ם\rb* \rb were dashed to pieces|רֻטָּֽשָׁה׃\rb*
\q2 \rb along with|עַל־\rb* \rb their children|בָּנִ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb Thus|כָּ֗כָה\rb* \rb it will be done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶם֙\rb*,\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb O Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your great|רָֽעַתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb wickedness|רָעַ֣ת\rb*.
\q1 \rb When the day dawns|בַּשַּׁ֕חַר\rb*,
\q2 \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb will be utterly cut off|נִדְמֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |נִדְמָ֖ה\rb*.
\c 11
\s1 Out of Egypt I Called My Son
\r (\ref Matthew 2:13–15|MAT 2:13-15\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb When|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb was a child|נַ֥עַר\rb*, \rb I loved him|וָאֹהֲבֵ֑הוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and out of Egypt|וּמִמִּצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb I called|קָרָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb My son|לִבְנִֽי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 11:1 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 2:15|MAT 2:15\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 2 \rb But the more I called|קָרְא֖וּ\rb* \rb Israel|לָהֶ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb the farther|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb they departed|הָלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb from Me|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*.\f + \fr 11:2 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa The more they called them, the more they went from them.\f*
\q1 \rb They sacrificed|יְזַבֵּ֔חוּ\rb* \rb to the Baals|לַבְּעָלִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and burned incense|יְקַטֵּרֽוּן׃\rb* \rb to carved images|וְלַפְּסִלִ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb It was I|וְאָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb who taught Ephraim|לְאֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb*\f + \fr 11:3 \ft That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verses 8, 9, and 12\f* \rb to walk|תִרְגַּ֙לְתִּי֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb taking them|קָחָ֖ם\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the arms|זְרֽוֹעֹתָ֑יו\rb*,
\q1 \rb but they never|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb realized|יָדְע֖וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb that it was I|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb who healed them|רְפָאתִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb I led them|אֶמְשְׁכֵם֙\rb* \rb with cords|בְּחַבְלֵ֨י\rb* \rb of kindness|אָדָ֤ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb with ropes|בַּעֲבֹת֣וֹת\rb* \rb of love|אַהֲבָ֔ה\rb*;
\q1 \rb |וָאֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb I lifted|כִּמְרִ֥ימֵי\rb* \rb the yoke|עֹ֖ל\rb* \rb from|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb their necks|לְחֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and bent down|וְאַ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb to feed them|אוֹכִֽיל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb Will they not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb return|יָשׁוּב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and be ruled|מַלְכּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb by Assyria|וְאַשּׁ֖וּר\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they refused|מֵאֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb to repent|לָשֽׁוּב׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 6 \rb A sword|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb will flash|וְחָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb through their cities|בְּעָרָ֔יו\rb*;
\q2 \rb it will destroy|וְכִלְּתָ֥ה\rb* \rb the bars of their gates|בַדָּ֖יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and consume them|וְאָכָ֑לָה\rb* \rb in their own plans|מִֽמֹּעֲצ֖וֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb My people|וְעַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb are bent|תְלוּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb on turning from Me|לִמְשֽׁוּבָתִ֑י\rb*.
\q2 \rb Though they call|יִקְרָאֻ֔הוּ\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the Most High|עַל֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb He will by no means|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |יַ֖חַד\rb* \rb exalt them|יְרוֹמֵם׃\rb*.
\s1 God’s Love for Israel
\q1 \v 8 \rb How|אֵ֞יךְ\rb* \rb could I give you up|אֶתֶּנְךָ֣\rb*, \rb O Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֗יִם\rb*?
\q2 \rb How could I surrender you|אֲמַגֶּנְךָ֙\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*?
\q1 \rb How|אֵ֚יךְ\rb* \rb could I make|אֶתֶּנְךָ֣\rb* \rb you like Admah|כְאַדְמָ֔ה\rb*?
\q2 \rb How could I treat|אֲשִֽׂימְךָ֖\rb* \rb you like Zeboiim|כִּצְבֹאיִ֑ם\rb*?
\q1 \rb My heart|לִבִּ֔י\rb* \rb is turned|נֶהְפַּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb within Me|עָלַי֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb My compassion|נִחוּמָֽי׃\rb* \rb is stirred|נִכְמְר֥וּ\rb*!
\q1 \v 9 \rb I will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb execute|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb the full fury|חֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of My anger|אַפִּ֔י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb destroy|לְשַׁחֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb again|אָשׁ֖וּב\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb am God|אֵ֤ל\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* —
\q2 \rb the Holy|קָד֔וֹשׁ\rb* \rb One among you|בְּקִרְבְּךָ֣\rb* —
\q2 \rb and I will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb come|אָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb in wrath|בְּעִֽיר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb They will walk after|אַחֲרֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יֵלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb He will roar|יִשְׁאָ֑ג\rb* \rb like a lion|כְּאַרְיֵ֣ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb roars|יִשְׁאַ֔ג\rb*,
\q2 \rb His children|בָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb will come trembling|וְיֶחֶרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb from the west|מִיָּֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb They will come trembling|יֶחֶרְד֤וּ\rb* \rb like birds|כְצִפּוֹר֙\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and like doves|וּכְיוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb*.
\q1 \rb Then I will settle them|וְהוֹשַׁבְתִּ֥ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their homes|בָּתֵּיהֶ֖ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb surrounds Me|סְבָבֻ֤נִי\rb* \rb with lies|בְכַ֙חַשׁ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb with deceit|וּבְמִרְמָ֖ה\rb*;
\q1 \rb but Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb still|עֹ֥ד\rb* \rb walks|רָד֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb God|אֵ֔ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and is faithful|נֶאֱמָֽן׃\rb* \rb to|וְעִם־\rb* \rb the Holy One|קְדוֹשִׁ֖ים\rb*.\f + \fr 11:12 \ft Or \fqa and Judah is unruly against God, the faithful Holy One\f*
\c 12
\s1 A Reproof of Ephraim, Judah, and Jacob
\q1 \v 1 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֜יִם\rb*\f + \fr 12:1 \ft That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verses 8 and 14\f* \rb feeds on|רֹעֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the wind|ר֙וּחַ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and pursues|וְרֹדֵ֣ף\rb* \rb the east wind|קָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb day long|הַיּ֕וֹם\rb*;
\q2 \rb he multiplies|יַרְבֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb lies|כָּזָ֥ב\rb* \rb and violence|וָשֹׁ֖ד\rb*;
\q1 \rb he makes|יִכְרֹ֔תוּ\rb* \rb a covenant|וּבְרִית֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Assyria|אַשּׁ֣וּר\rb*
\q2 \rb and sends|יוּבָֽל׃\rb* \rb olive oil|וְשֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb to Egypt|לְמִצְרַ֥יִם\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb The LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has a charge to bring|וְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*.
\q2 \rb He will punish|וְלִפְקֹ֤ד\rb*\rb |עַֽל־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹב֙\rb*\f + \fr 12:2 \fqa Jacob \ft means \fqa he grasps the heel \ft or \fqa he deceives\ft .\f* \rb according to his ways|כִּדְרָכָ֔יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and repay|יָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb according to his deeds|כְּמַעֲלָלָ֖יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb In the womb|בַּבֶּ֖טֶן\rb* \rb he grasped his brother’s|אָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb heel|עָקַ֣ב\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb and in his vigor|וּבְאוֹנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb he wrestled|שָׂרָ֥ה\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb Yes, he struggled|וָיָּ֤שַׂר\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאָךְ֙\rb*\f + \fr 12:4 \ft Or \fqa Angel\f* \rb and prevailed|וַיֻּכָ֔ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb he wept|בָּכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and sought His favor|וַיִּתְחַנֶּן־\rb*;
\q1 \rb he found Him|יִמְצָאֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb at Bethel|אֵל֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and spoke|יְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with Him|עִמָּֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb there|וְשָׁ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 12:4 \ft LXX and Syriac; MT \fqa and there He spoke with us\f* —
\q1 \v 5 \rb the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Hosts|הַצְּבָא֑וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is His name of renown|זִכְרֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb But you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb must return|תָשׁ֑וּב\rb* \rb to your God|בֵּאלֹהֶ֣יךָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb maintain|שְׁמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb love|חֶ֤סֶד\rb* \rb and justice|וּמִשְׁפָּט֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and always|תָּמִֽיד׃\rb* \rb wait|וְקַוֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb A merchant|כְּנַ֗עַן\rb* \rb loves|אָהֵֽב׃\rb* \rb to defraud|לַעֲשֹׁ֥ק\rb*
\q2 \rb with dishonest|מִרְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb scales|מֹאזְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb in his hands|בְּיָד֛וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb And Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb boasts|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*: “\rb |אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb How rich I have become|עָשַׁ֔רְתִּי\rb*!
\q2 \rb I have found|מָצָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb wealth|א֖וֹן\rb* \rb for myself|לִ֑י\rb*.
\q1 \rb In all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my labors|יְגִיעַ֕י\rb*, \rb they can find|יִמְצְאוּ־\rb* \rb in me|לִ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb iniquity|עָוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb sinful|חֵֽטְא׃\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb But I am|וְאָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb ever since the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will again make you dwell|אוֹשִֽׁיבְךָ֥\rb*\rb |עֹ֛ד\rb* \rb in tents|בָאֳהָלִ֖ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb as in the days|כִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the appointed feast|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb I spoke|וְדִבַּ֙רְתִּי֙\rb* \rb through|עַל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb multiplied|הִרְבֵּ֑יתִי\rb* \rb their visions|חָז֣וֹן\rb*;
\q2 \rb I gave parables|אֲדַמֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb through|וּבְיַ֥ד\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb Is there|אִם־\rb* \rb iniquity|אָ֙וֶן֙\rb* \rb in Gilead|גִּלְעָ֥ד\rb*?
\q2 \rb They will surely|אַךְ־\rb* \rb come|הָי֔וּ\rb* \rb to nothing|שָׁ֣וְא\rb*.
\q1 \rb Do they sacrifice|זִבֵּ֑חוּ\rb* \rb bulls|שְׁוָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb in Gilgal|בַּגִּלְגָּ֖ל\rb*?
\q2 \rb Indeed|גַּ֤ם\rb*, \rb their altars will be|מִזְבְּחוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb heaps of stones|כְּגַלִּ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb in|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the furrows|תַּלְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the field|שָׂדָֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb fled|וַיִּבְרַ֥ח\rb* \rb to the land|שְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 12:12 \ft That is, northwest Mesopotamia\f*
\q2 \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb worked|וַיַּעֲבֹ֤ד\rb* \rb for a wife|בְּאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* —
\q2 \rb for a wife|וּבְאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb he tended sheep|שָׁמָֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb But by a prophet|וּבְנָבִ֕יא\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלָ֧ה\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and by a prophet|וּבְנָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb he was preserved|נִשְׁמָֽר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb has provoked bitter|תַּמְרוּרִ֑ים\rb* \rb anger|הִכְעִ֥יס\rb*,
\q2 \rb so his Lord|אֲדֹנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb will leave|יִטּ֔וֹשׁ\rb* \rb his bloodguilt|וְדָמָיו֙\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and repay|יָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb for his contempt|וְחֶ֨רְפָּת֔וֹ\rb*.
\c 13
\s1 God’s Anger against Israel
\q1 \v 1 \rb When Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*\f + \fr 13:1 \ft That is, the northern kingdom of Israel; also in verse 12\f* \rb spoke|כְּדַבֵּ֤ר\rb*, \rb there was trembling|רְתֵ֔ת\rb*;
\q2 \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb was exalted|נָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.
\q1 \rb But he incurred guilt|וַיֶּאְשַׁ֥ם\rb* \rb through Baal|בַּבַּ֖עַל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb they sin|לַחֲטֹ֗א\rb* \rb more and more|יוֹסִ֣פוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and make|וַיַּעְשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶם֩\rb* \rb cast images|מַסֵּכָ֨ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb idols|עֲצַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb skillfully made|כִּתְבוּנָם֙\rb* \rb from their silver|מִכַּסְפָּ֤ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb all|כֻּלֹּ֑ה\rb* \rb of them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of craftsmen|חָרָשִׁ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb People|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb say of them|אֹמְרִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 “\rb They offer human sacrifice|זֹבְחֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אָדָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and kiss|יִשָּׁקֽוּן׃\rb* \rb the calves|עֲגָלִ֖ים\rb*!”\f + \fr 13:2 \ft Or \fqa “The men who sacrifice kiss the calves!”\ft See \ref 1 Kings 19:18|1KI 19:18\ref*.\f*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb they will be|יִֽהְיוּ֙\rb* \rb like the morning|בֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb mist|כַּעֲנַן־\rb*,
\q2 \rb like the early|מַשְׁכִּ֣ים\rb* \rb dew|וְכַטַּ֖ל\rb* \rb that vanishes|הֹלֵ֑ךְ\rb*,
\q1 \rb like chaff|כְּמֹץ֙\rb* \rb blown|יְסֹעֵ֣ר\rb* \rb from a threshing floor|מִגֹּ֔רֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb like smoke|וּכְעָשָׁ֖ן\rb* \rb through an open window|מֵאֲרֻבָּֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Yet I am|וְאָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb ever since the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*;
\q1 \rb you know|תֵדָ֔ע\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb God|וֵאלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb but Me|זֽוּלָתִי֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb for there is no|אַ֖יִן\rb* \rb Savior|וּמוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb* \rb besides Me|בִּלְתִּֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb knew you|יְדַעְתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of drought|תַּלְאֻבֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb When they had pasture|כְּמַרְעִיתָם֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb they became satisfied|וַיִּשְׂבָּ֔עוּ\rb*;
\q1 \rb when they were satisfied|שָׂבְע֖וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb their hearts|לִבָּ֑ם\rb* \rb became proud|וַיָּ֣רָם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and as a result|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb they forgot Me|שְׁכֵחֽוּנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb So like|כְּמוֹ־\rb* \rb a lion|שָׁ֑חַל\rb* \rb I will pounce|וָאֱהִ֥י\rb* \rb on them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb like a leopard|כְּנָמֵ֖ר\rb* \rb I will lurk|אָשֽׁוּר׃\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the path|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Like a bear|כְּדֹ֣ב\rb* \rb robbed of her cubs|שַׁכּ֔וּל\rb* \rb I will attack them|אֶפְגְּשֵׁם֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I will tear|וְאֶקְרַ֖ע\rb* \rb open their chests|סְג֣וֹר\rb*\rb |לִבָּ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb There|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb I will devour them|וְאֹכְלֵ֥ם\rb* \rb like a lion|כְּלָבִ֔יא\rb*,
\q2 \rb like a wild|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb tearing them apart|תְּבַקְּעֵֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 Death and Resurrection
\r (\ref 1 Corinthians 15:50–58|1CO 15:50-58\ref*)
\q1 \v 9 \rb You are destroyed|שִֽׁחֶתְךָ֥\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb because you are|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb against Me|בִ֥י\rb* —
\q2 \rb against your helper|בְעֶזְרֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Where is|אֱהִ֤י\rb* \rb your king|מַלְכְּךָ֙\rb* \rb now|אֵפ֔וֹא\rb*\f + \fr 13:10 \ft Or \fqa Shall I be your King now\f*
\q2 \rb to save you|וְיוֹשִֽׁיעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your cities|עָרֶ֑יךָ\rb*,
\q1 \rb and the rulers|וְשֹׁ֣פְטֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you said|אָמַ֔רְתָּ\rb*,
\q2 “\rb Give|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֖י\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and princes|וְשָׂרִֽים׃\rb*”?
\q1 \v 11 \rb So in My anger|בְּאַפִּ֔י\rb* \rb I gave|אֶֽתֶּן־\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and in My wrath|בְּעֶבְרָתִֽי׃ס\rb* \rb I took him away|וְאֶקַּ֖ח\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb The iniquity|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֔יִם\rb* \rb is bound up|צָרוּר֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb his sin|חַטָּאתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb is stored up|צְפוּנָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb Labor|יֽוֹלֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb pains|חֶבְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb come|יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb upon him|ל֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he is|הוּא־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb an unwise|חָכָ֔ם\rb* \rb son|בֵן֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the time arrives|עֵ֥ת\rb*,
\q2 \rb he|בָּנִֽים׃\rb* \rb fails|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to present himself|יַעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb at the opening of the womb|בְּמִשְׁבַּ֥ר\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb I will ransom them|אֶפְדֵּ֔ם\rb* \rb from the power|מִיַּ֤ד\rb* \rb of Sheol|שְׁאוֹל֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will redeem them|אֶגְאָלֵ֑ם\rb* \rb from Death|מִמָּ֖וֶת\rb*.\f + \fr 13:14 \ft Or \fqa Shall I ransom them from the power of Sheol? Shall I redeem them from Death?\f*
\q1 \rb Where|אֱהִ֨י\rb*, \rb O Death|מָ֗וֶת\rb*, \rb are your plagues|דְבָרֶיךָ֜\rb*?
\q2 \rb Where|אֱהִ֤י\rb*, \rb O Sheol|שְׁא֔וֹל\rb*, \rb is your sting|קָֽטָבְךָ֙\rb*?\f + \fr 13:14 \ft LXX \fqa Where, O Death, is your penalty? Where, O Hades, is your sting?\ft Cited in \ref 1 Corinthians 15:55|1CO 15:55\ref*\f*
\b 
\q1 \rb Compassion|נֹ֖חַם\rb* \rb is hidden|יִסָּתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb from My eyes|מֵעֵינָֽי׃\rb*.
\s1 Judgment on Samaria
\q1 \v 15 \rb Although|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb flourishes|יַפְרִ֑יא\rb* \rb among|בֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb his brothers|אַחִ֖ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb an east wind|קָדִים֩\rb* \rb will come|יָב֣וֹא\rb* —
\q1 \rb a wind|ר֨וּחַ\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*
\q2 \rb rising up|עֹלֶ֗ה\rb* \rb from the desert|מִמִּדְבָּ֣ר\rb*.
\q1 \rb His fountain|מְקוֹרוֹ֙\rb* \rb will fail|וְיֵב֤וֹשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and his spring|מַעְיָנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb will run dry|וְיֶחֱרַ֣ב\rb*.
\q1 \rb The wind|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb will plunder|יִשְׁסֶ֔ה\rb* \rb his treasury|אוֹצַ֖ר\rb*
\q2 \rb of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb precious|חֶמְדָּֽה׃\rb* \rb article|כְּלִ֥י\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb Samaria|שֹֽׁמְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb will bear her guilt|תֶּאְשַׁם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she has rebelled|מָרְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb against her God|בֵּֽאלֹהֶ֑יהָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb They will fall|יִפֹּ֔לוּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb*;
\q2 \rb their little ones|עֹלְלֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb will be dashed to pieces|יְרֻטָּ֔שׁוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and their pregnant|וְהָרִיּוֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb women ripped open|יְבֻקָּֽעוּ׃פ\rb*.
\c 14
\s1 A Call to Repentance
\r (\ref Jeremiah 3:11–25|JER 3:11-25\ref*; \ref Zechariah 1:1–6|ZEC 1:1-6\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Return|שׁ֚וּבָה\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have stumbled|כָשַׁ֖לְתָּ\rb* \rb by your iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb Bring|קְח֤וּ\rb* \rb your|עִמָּכֶם֙\rb* \rb confessions|דְּבָרִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and return|וְשׁ֖וּבוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb Say|אִמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to Him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*: “\rb Take away|תִּשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb our iniquity|עָוֺן֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and receive|וְקַח־\rb* \rb us graciously|ט֔וֹב\rb*,
\q1 \rb that we may present|וּֽנְשַׁלְּמָ֥ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the fruit|פָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb of our lips|שְׂפָתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 14:2 \ft LXX and Syriac; Hebrew \fqa that we may present our lips as sacrificial bulls\f*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Assyria|אַשּׁ֣וּר׀\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb save us|יוֹשִׁיעֵ֗נוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb nor will we|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb ride|נִרְכָּ֔ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb horses|סוּס֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb We will never again|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb say|נֹ֥אמַר\rb*, ‘\rb Our gods|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*!’
\q2 \rb to the work|לְמַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of our own hands|יָדֵ֑ינוּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb For|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in You|בְּךָ֖\rb* \rb the fatherless|יָתֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb find compassion|יְרֻחַ֥ם\rb*.”
\s1 A Promise of God’s Blessing
\q1 \v 4 \rb I will heal|אֶרְפָּא֙\rb* \rb their apostasy|מְשׁ֣וּבָתָ֔ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will freely|נְדָבָ֑ה\rb* \rb love them|אֹהֲבֵ֖ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb My anger|אַפִּ֖י\rb* \rb has turned away|שָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb from them|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb I will be|אֶהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb like the dew|כַטַּל֙\rb* \rb to Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb he will blossom|יִפְרַ֖ח\rb* \rb like the lily|כַּשּֽׁוֹשַׁנָּ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and take|וְיַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb root|שָׁרָשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb like the cedars of Lebanon|כַּלְּבָנֽוֹן׃\rb*.
